--- Invokes a named method on an object with a secure call barrier that prevents errors or taint from function lookup and execution from propagating to the caller.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `object`: The table on which to look up the named method from. Lookup of the method uses raw access and ignores any associated metatable.
--- - `method`: The name of a method to retrieve.
--- - `arguments`: Arguments to supply to the method. The initial 'object' parameter is always supplied as the first argument, followed by these values.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `results`: Results from the executed function. If an error occurred, this result list will be empty.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_securecallmethod)
declare function securecallmethod(object: unknown, method: string, ...: unknown): (...unknown)
--- Securely copies a Lua value. Tables are deep-copied with recursive and shared references preserved; script objects are preserved by reference. Copied values receive the current execution taint.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `value`: The Lua value to copy.
--- - `options`: Optional settings controlling value copying behavior. If omitted, default secure copy options are used.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `copy`: The copied value. For tables, recursive and shared references within the copied graph are preserved.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_securecopy)
declare function securecopy(value: unknown?, options: SecureCopyOptions?): unknown
