--- Returns information about the spell currently being cast by the specified unit.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `name`: The name of the spell, or nil if no spell is being cast.
--- - `displayName`: The name to be displayed.
--- - `textureID`: The texture path associated with the spell icon.
--- - `startTimeMs`: Specifies when casting began in milliseconds (corresponds to GetTime()*1000).
--- - `endTimeMs`: Specifies when casting will end in milliseconds (corresponds to GetTime()*1000).
--- - `isTradeskill`: Specifies if the cast is a tradeskill
--- - `castID`: GUID - The unique identifier for this spell cast, for example `Cast-3-3890-1159-21205-8936-00014B7E7F`.
--- - `notInterruptible`: if true, indicates that this cast cannot be interrupted with abilities like Kick or Pummel. In default UI those spells have shield frame around their icons on enemy cast bars. Always returns `nil` in Classic .
--- - `castingSpellID`: The spell's unique identifier.
--- - `delayTimeMs`: Total accrued delay for this spell cast from pushback.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_UnitCastingInfo)
declare function UnitCastingInfo(unit: string): (string | Secret<string>, string | Secret<string>, number | Secret<number>, number | Secret<number>, number | Secret<number>, boolean | Secret<boolean>, string | Secret<string>, (boolean | Secret<boolean>)?, number | Secret<number>, (number | Secret<number>)?, number | Secret<number>)
--- Returns the duration of the spell the unit channels, or nil if it channels none.
