--- Returns information about the spell currently being channeled by the specified unit.
---
--- **Returns**
--- - `name`: The name of the spell, or nil if no spell is being channeled.
--- - `displayName`: The name to be displayed.
--- - `textureID`: The texture path associated with the spell icon.
--- - `startTimeMs`: Specifies when channeling began, in milliseconds (corresponds to GetTime()*1000).
--- - `endTimeMs`: Specifies when channeling will end, in in milliseconds (corresponds to GetTime()*1000).
--- - `isTradeskill`: Specifies if the cast is a tradeskill.
--- - `notInterruptible`: if true, indicates that this channeling cannot be interrupted with abilities like Kick or Pummel. In default UI those spells have shield frame around their icons on enemy channeling bars. Always returns `nil` in Classic .
--- - `spellID`: The spell's unique identifier.
---
--- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_UnitChannelInfo)
declare function UnitChannelInfo(unit: string): (string | Secret<string>, string | Secret<string>, number | Secret<number>, number | Secret<number>, number | Secret<number>, boolean | Secret<boolean>, (boolean | Secret<boolean>)?, number | Secret<number>, boolean | Secret<boolean>, number | Secret<number>, (number | Secret<number>)?)
