    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.GetExportAvailability)
    function GetExportAvailability(): HousingResult
    --- Returns success if Blueprints as a feature is currently enabled and available
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.GetFeatureAvailability)
    function GetFeatureAvailability(): HousingResult
    --- Returns success if the player can currently import Blueprints, or a specific error type (ex: invalid location or permissions)
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.GetImportAvailability)
    function GetImportAvailability(): HousingResult
    --- Imports the specified blueprint, if available (see IsImportAvailable and CanImportTypeFromCurrentLocation); Listen for HousingBlueprintImportSuccess and HousingBlueprintImportFailure for results
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.ImportBlueprint)
    function ImportBlueprint(shareCode: string)
    --- Returns true if the string matches the valid expected format for a Blueprint Share Code; Does NOT check whether the shareCode actually matches up to a real valid Blueprint
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.IsShareCodeValid)
    function IsShareCodeValid(shareCode: string): boolean
    --- Rename the specified owned blueprint to the specified name; Listen for HousingBlueprintRenameSuccess and HousingBlueprintRenameFailure for results
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.RenameBlueprint)
    function RenameBlueprint(blueprintID: number, newName: string)
    --- Request the full list of all of the player's Blueprints; This is async, either the HOUSING_BLUEPRINT_COLLECTION_RECEIVED or HOUSING_BLUEPRINT_COLLECTION_FAILURE event will eventually be fired as a result
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.RequestBlueprintCollection)
    function RequestBlueprintCollection()
    --- Request the full contents of a specific Blueprint, in context of the current owned plot or house (if any); This is async as content info includes dynamic data from the server, either the HOUSING_BLUEPRINT_CONTENTS_RECEIVED or HOUSING_BLUEPRINT_CONTENTS_FAILURE event will eventually be fired as a result; Calling this again before a prior request has finished will cancel the prior request
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.RequestBlueprintContents)
    function RequestBlueprintContents(shareCode: string)
    --- Request the full contents of a specific Blueprint, either in context of a specific owned House or plot, or explicitly outside of any specific context; Typically used to update missing requirement info from previously-retrieved contents; See RequestBlueprintContents for other notes
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.RequestBlueprintContentsForContext)
    function RequestBlueprintContentsForContext(shareCode: string, optionalHouseGUID: string?)
    --- Start the process of importing a Room Blueprint. This will lead to Layout Mode being opened, so the player can then select an available door to attach the room to
    ---
    --- [warcraft.wiki.gg](https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API_C_HousingBlueprint.StartImportRoomBlueprint)
    function StartImportRoomBlueprint(shareCode: string)
    --- Returns the blueprint share code read from the entered text, or nothing.
