--- Fires when a message is posted to a chat channel the player is in, such as General or Trade.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `bnSenderID`: The sender's Battle.net account ID, for Battle.net messages.
--- - `channelBaseName`: The channel's name without its number, for channel messages.
--- - `channelIndex`: The channel's number in the player's channel list, for channel messages.
--- - `channelName`: The channel's full name, with its number, for channel messages; otherwise an empty string.
--- - `discordInfo`: Details of the Discord user, for messages relayed from Discord.
--- - `guid`: The sender's GUID.
--- - `hideSenderInLetterbox`: Whether the message belongs only in the cinematic letterbox; Blizzard's chat frames skip it.
--- - `isMobile`: Whether the sender is using the mobile app.
--- - `languageID`: The ID of the language the message is in.
--- - `languageName`: The language the message is in, or an empty string.
--- - `lineID`: The chat line's ID, for the `C_ChatInfo` chat-line functions.
--- - `playerName`: The sender's name.
--- - `specialFlags`: The sender's flag, such as `"GM"`, `"GUIDE"` or `"NEWCOMER"`, or an empty string.
--- - `suppressRaidIcons`: Whether raid target expressions such as `{star}` in the text are left as text.
--- - `text`: The message text.
--- - `zoneChannelID`: The ID of the zone channel the message came through, or 0.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
