---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event PLAYER_TOTEM_UPDATE(totemSlot: number)
--- Fires when a spell flyout changes. Blizzard updates the flyout buttons and the action buttons that hold that flyout.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `flyoutID`: The flyout that changed.
--- - `isLearned`: Whether that spell is learned.
--- - `spellID`: The spell in the flyout that changed.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_FLYOUT_UPDATE(flyoutID: number?, spellID: number?, isLearned: boolean?)
--- Fires when the game places a newly learned spell on the player's action bar. Blizzard plays the icon fly-in animation to that slot.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `page`: The action bar page.
--- - `slot`: The action slot the spell was placed in; it may be `0` when the gamepad interface is enabled.
--- - `spellID`: The spell.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_PUSHED_TO_ACTIONBAR(spellID: number, slot: number, page: number)
--- Fires when the game places a newly learned spell into a flyout on the player's action bar. Blizzard plays the icon fly-in animation.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `flyoutPage`: The action bar page.
--- - `flyoutSlot`: The action slot of the flyout.
--- - `spellID`: The spell.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_PUSHED_TO_FLYOUT_ON_ACTIONBAR(spellID: number, flyoutSlot: number, flyoutPage: number)
--- Fires when the charges of one of the player's spells change. Blizzard's action buttons update their count.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_UPDATE_CHARGES()
--- Fires when the cooldown of one of the player's spells changes. Blizzard's action buttons and cooldown displays refresh their cooldowns.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `spellID`: Can be a base spell or an override spell. A nil value indicates that all cooldowns should be updated, rather than just a specific one.
--- - `baseSpellID`: Will be set to the base spell if the spellID parameter is an override spell.
--- - `category`: If the spellID parameter is set, the cooldown category of the spell. A nil value indicates the spell does not have a cooldown category.
--- - `startRecoveryCategory`: If the spellID parameter is set, the cooldown start recovery category of the spell. A nil value indicates the spell does not have a cooldown start recovery category.
--- - `itemID`: If the itemID parameter is set, it's the itemID associated with the cast of the spell.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_UPDATE_COOLDOWN(spellID: number?, baseSpellID: number?, category: number?, startRecoveryCategory: number?, itemID: number?)
--- Fires when the icon of one of the player's spells changes. Blizzard's action buttons and cooldown viewer refresh their icons.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `spellID`: Always refers to the base spell. A nil value indicates that all icons should be updated, rather than just a specific one.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_UPDATE_ICON(spellID: number?)
--- Fires when the usability of the player's spells changes. Blizzard's flyout buttons and cooldown viewer update.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_UPDATE_USABLE()
--- Fires when the remaining uses of one of the player's spells change. Blizzard's cooldown viewer updates.
---
--- **Parameters**
--- - `spellID`: Can be a base spell or override spell.
--- - `baseSpellID`: Will be set to the base spell if the spellID parameter is an override spell.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELL_UPDATE_USES(spellID: number, baseSpellID: number?)
--- Fires when the player's spells change, such as after learning or unlearning a spell or changing specialization. Many Blizzard frames refresh on it, among them the spellbook and the stable.
---
--- *Description by wowlua: the API's documentation has none.*
declare event SPELLS_CHANGED()
